    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "finger ring: a ring worn on the finger (Latin anulus), of gold, silver or base metal, often gilded and set with precious stones — rubies, balas rubies, sapphires, emeralds, turquoises, pearls, garnets or diamonds — or with glass paste; quality ranges from coarse to fine. The English forms ring/ringes are shared with the generic ring concept." ;
